    "provinceDeepAtlasProfile": {
      "oneLine": "Aelwynora is centered at 61.114097, -25.982066 under Consensus Democracy, with 47,825,000 people across 11 settlements.",
      "extremeAtlasDescription": "Aelwynora occupies 5,226,112.83 sq mi / 13,535,570.09 sq km of modeled Earth-sized territory, about 2.653691% of Belavadös's surface. It is not merely a province but a continent-scale civic machine: Beach and grass with water, Partial forest and Ocean Surface floating settlement define its broad terrain, while its settlements intensify into Beach and grass with water, Ocean Surface floating settlement, Farming, Hybrid tree and forest floor and Beach and reefs with water. Population density is 3.533 people/sq km / 9.151 people/sq mi, which lets wilderness, roads, faction-held corridors, and vast uncrowded borders remain huge.",
      "peopleFactionsAndFaith": "The strongest public people-groups are Humans, Near-Humans, and Mixed Heritage, Halfling and Smallfolk, Animalfolk and Mammalian Anthropomorphs, Elf Parent Race and Elf Bloodlines, Amphibious and Aquatic Peoples, Fey and Trickster Folk, and 2 more. Frequently recorded peoples include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Harengon, Elf — Wood Elf, Elf — Eladrin, Fey-Folk — Faerie, Satyr, Changeling, and 4 more. Faction visibility leans toward The Choral Synod and The Regent Lattice, with worship and patronage records naming Nebyrr, Ishtanora, Iskareth, Bastveig, Sokhivar, Raeshkul, Sigrananna, and 3 more.",
      "groupLinkDescription": "The province participates in 21 recorded four-province geography group links, including 18 cross-transportation-group links. These links place it inside overlapping regional corridors rather than one isolated block, allowing border-adjacent transit, faction influence, and cultural spillover to breathe across group lines.",
